      "action": "manual",
      "code": "database_lost",
      "manual_text": "Stop every unblock process. Restore the database file from a backup or from the newest .unblock/.recovery/<run>/snapshot.db by copying it to the configured database path; the snapshot is a complete VACUUM INTO copy carrying its schema stamp. Before restoring, with every unblock process stopped, move any -wal, -shm or -journal file left beside the database path into a new directory under .unblock/.recovery/, because a stale -wal is replayed into a restored file on its first open. Otherwise, after moving those files aside the same way, run `unblock init`, whose database-only mode creates an empty database under the configured db_filename, keeps config.toml and refuses while any such file remains, then import the last export through an MCP client's `sync` tool `import` action; the CLI has no import command.",
      "path": "manual",
